[rain pattering]

254
00:14:15.000 --> 00:14:16.360
- You okay?
- Yeah. I'm okay.

255
00:14:16.440 --> 00:14:17.520
Are you hurt?

256
00:14:19.880 --> 00:14:22.080
Why didn't you answer me on the radio?

257
00:14:22.160 --> 00:14:24.080
I was too close to the suspect. David.

258
00:14:24.160 --> 00:14:26.560
In what world do you go after a guy
when you're unarmed?

259
00:14:26.640 --> 00:14:27.960
In what world?!

260
00:14:28.640 --> 00:14:30.560
Did you forget all your training?

261
00:14:31.520 --> 00:14:33.040
Are you out of your mind?

262
00:14:34.600 --> 00:14:36.120
Did we arrest the guy or what?

263
00:14:43.440 --> 00:14:46.520
The next time I tell you to stay
at the base. you stay at the base.

264
00:14:52.600 --> 00:14:54.680
[police sirens wailing in distance]

265
00:14:56.400 --> 00:14:57.600
What's wrong?

266
00:14:58.200 --> 00:14:59.280
Look.

267
00:14:59.360 --> 00:15:03.280
If you're ever thinking of bringing a guy
from my section. tell me first. okay?

268
00:15:03.360 --> 00:15:06.080
I ordered him to stay at the station
and get a medical.

269
00:15:06.160 --> 00:15:07.600
- A medical?
- Yeah. a medical.

270
00:15:07.680 --> 00:15:10.320
We always take the new guys out on ops
and we never ask permission.

271
00:15:10.400 --> 00:15:12.240
Don't tell me you've never done it.

272
00:15:13.760 --> 00:15:16.120
Max has zero experience in the field.

273
00:15:16.200 --> 00:15:19.000
It doesn't make sense to put him
in a risky operation his first time out.

274
00:15:19.080 --> 00:15:21.240
But you put the other newbies
on the assault squad.

275
00:15:21.320 --> 00:15:23.800
It's too much for him to do
plain clothes surveillance?

276
00:15:23.880 --> 00:15:26.560
You know. run your section how you want
and let me handle mine. okay?

277
00:15:26.640 --> 00:15:29.120
Hold on! If it wasn't for Max.
we wouldn't have made the arrest.

278
00:15:29.200 --> 00:15:32.200
- Whatever!
- What the hell's wrong with you. man?

279
00:15:34.680 --> 00:15:36.000
Yeah. send me that.

280
00:15:36.920 --> 00:15:37.760
That one too.

281
00:15:37.840 --> 00:15:40.360
- We'll need to check all of this.
- And that one.

282
00:15:40.440 --> 00:15:42.840
- [CÃ©dric] Major Bonenfant.
- Commander Saint-Juste. Inspection.

283
00:15:43.800 --> 00:15:44.840
[speaking indistinctly]

284
00:15:45.960 --> 00:15:47.280
- Hello.
- [man] Pleased to meet you.

285
00:15:56.520 --> 00:15:59.280
[police siren wailing in distance]

286
00:16:04.960 --> 00:16:05.880
[exhales]

287
00:16:10.840 --> 00:16:11.720
Who's your boss?

288
00:16:13.160 --> 00:16:14.080
Oh. big man. huh?

289
00:16:14.160 --> 00:16:15.720
Thirty against one.

290
00:16:16.240 --> 00:16:17.840
Dressed up like little boy scouts.

291
00:16:17.920 --> 00:16:19.480
Yeah. Give me a name.

292
00:16:19.560 --> 00:16:22.600
And that other guy. your little pal there.
before you jumped out.

293
00:16:22.680 --> 00:16:24.880
all 30 of you. from your clown cars.

294
00:16:24.960 --> 00:16:26.040
That guy?

295
00:16:26.960 --> 00:16:28.120
I'll smoke him.

296
00:16:31.760 --> 00:16:33.600
Oh yeah? You'll smoke him?

297
00:16:35.040 --> 00:16:38.040
[ominous music playing]

298
00:16:44.920 --> 00:16:46.280
Have a good look.

299
00:16:48.360 --> 00:16:49.840
[breathes heavily]

300
00:16:49.920 --> 00:16:53.360
The only reason you're alive is because
the unit has a strong sense of discipline.

301
00:16:53.840 --> 00:16:56.160
You know what I'm talking about.
You served your country.

302
00:16:57.800 --> 00:16:59.560
But I've got some bad news for you.

303
00:17:01.560 --> 00:17:04.120
I have a hard time following the rules.

304
00:17:05.760 --> 00:17:07.360
And if you don't play ballâ€¦

305
00:17:11.400 --> 00:17:14.560
I promise you it'll be a real pleasure
to show you what I meant by that.

306
00:17:14.640 --> 00:17:16.240
[tense music playing]

307
00:17:16.320 --> 00:17:18.160
I'm wondering
how much pain you can tolerate.

308
00:17:18.240 --> 00:17:19.080
[grunts]

309
00:17:19.560 --> 00:17:21.080
You gonna talk now or what?

310
00:17:21.160 --> 00:17:23.120
- [grunts]
- [CÃ©dric] What're you doing? Let him go!

311
00:17:23.200 --> 00:17:25.080
Close your eyes! Close your eyes!
Cover them!

312
00:17:25.160 --> 00:17:26.960
- Out!
- [suspect] Get off me! Get off me!

313
00:17:27.040 --> 00:17:28.360
[struggling]

314
00:17:28.440 --> 00:17:31.280
- [CÃ©dric] Shut the fuck up.
- [suspect grunts and yells]

315
00:17:31.880 --> 00:17:33.560
[panting]

316
00:17:33.640 --> 00:17:34.960
[groans]

317
00:17:39.120 --> 00:17:40.840
[David] Are you down there?

318
00:17:40.920 --> 00:17:43.600
- So is he awake?
- Yeah.

319
00:17:45.360 --> 00:17:47.600
Okay. I'll see you at the hospital.
I gotta go.

320
00:17:49.040 --> 00:17:50.320
Commander Saint-Juste.

321
00:17:50.920 --> 00:17:52.520
General Inspection.

322
00:17:52.600 --> 00:17:54.640
I'm aware of who you are
and what kind of work you do.

323
00:17:54.720 --> 00:17:57.760
You think I'm just a pain in the ass
but I'm here to protect you from yourself.

324
00:17:57.840 --> 00:17:59.080
[scoffs]

325
00:17:59.160 --> 00:18:01.160
Okay. How helpful.

326
00:18:01.240 --> 00:18:03.440
Your job here is tactical only.

327
00:18:04.120 --> 00:18:05.560
Not investigating.

328
00:18:05.640 --> 00:18:07.840
And definitely not intimidating suspects.

329
00:18:07.920 --> 00:18:11.160
If this case falls apart due to
your display of excess testosteroneâ€¦

330
00:18:12.880 --> 00:18:15.480
you'll have to find
a new career. Commander.

331
00:18:20.360 --> 00:18:22.960
[officer] Yeah. Try to get another angle.

332
00:18:24.080 --> 00:18:25.760
[sighs]

333
00:18:26.360 --> 00:18:27.880
[PJ] Ah. here he is.

334
00:18:27.960 --> 00:18:29.800
- What's up. handsome?
- [Max chuckles]

335
00:18:32.000 --> 00:18:34.080
- You good. Rapha?
- Yeah.

336
00:18:34.800 --> 00:18:37.280
Looks like you missed
your calling in Intel.

337
00:18:37.360 --> 00:18:38.200
[Rapha chuckles]

338
00:18:38.280 --> 00:18:41.120
I'm sure I didn't score
points with David. you know?

339
00:18:41.200 --> 00:18:44.440
In the end. you're the guy who went
after the terrorist. so take the win.

340
00:18:45.120 --> 00:18:46.520
How'd you end up with Intel?

341
00:18:46.600 --> 00:18:48.520
I go where I'm needed. dude.

342
00:18:48.600 --> 00:18:50.760
Not my style to sit on the bench
when the game's on.

343
00:18:50.840 --> 00:18:53.440
This guy's ego's growing by the minute.
[laughs]

344
00:18:53.520 --> 00:18:55.000
Lucky I didn't wait for you guys.

345
00:18:55.080 --> 00:18:57.480
He's been full of himself from the start.
He was born that way.

346
00:18:57.560 --> 00:18:59.440
- The little prick.
- [Rapha and PJ laugh]

347
00:19:07.200 --> 00:19:09.280
Excuse me. where do I find
the intensive care unit?

348
00:19:09.360 --> 00:19:11.360
- Down the end on your left.
- Thanks.

349
00:19:16.080 --> 00:19:17.400
[officer] Can I help you. sir?

350
00:19:18.320 --> 00:19:19.320
Okay.

351
00:19:29.400 --> 00:19:31.400
[speaking indistinctly]

352
00:19:56.920 --> 00:19:57.800
[David sighs]

353
00:20:02.560 --> 00:20:04.560
So. how's he doing?

354
00:20:04.640 --> 00:20:06.840
[Jess sighs] They put him
in an induced coma.

355
00:20:08.800 --> 00:20:11.000
They say everything depends
on the next 24 hours.

356
00:20:14.560 --> 00:20:15.520
And you?

357
00:20:23.240 --> 00:20:25.720
Truth is. not great. Not great.

358
00:20:28.360 --> 00:20:29.760
[poignant music playing]

359
00:20:29.840 --> 00:20:31.280
I called Manon this morning.

360
00:20:32.520 --> 00:20:36.560
I told her it might be good for us
to spend more time together.

361
00:20:38.600 --> 00:20:40.960
So we're seeing each other
tomorrow for lunch.

362
00:20:42.000 --> 00:20:43.040
And. uhâ€¦

363
00:20:46.840 --> 00:20:48.400
I was thinking. if you're free.

364
00:20:49.640 --> 00:20:52.720
you'd come with us.
so we can be together. The three of us.

365
00:20:53.880 --> 00:20:55.560
[sighs] Mm. Come on. David.

366
00:20:55.640 --> 00:20:58.680
We can't keep acting
like everything's normal between us.

367
00:20:59.920 --> 00:21:01.440
I'm moving to Singapore.

368
00:21:01.520 --> 00:21:03.400
We have to tell her at some point.

369
00:21:05.360 --> 00:21:07.000
At some point. yeah.

370
00:21:07.080 --> 00:21:08.000
There's no rush.

371
00:21:09.480 --> 00:21:12.280
Yes. but she'll need time
to think about what she wants.

372
00:21:14.160 --> 00:21:16.440
Who says there's
anything for her to think about?

373
00:21:17.640 --> 00:21:18.840
This is where Manon's life is.

374
00:21:18.920 --> 00:21:21.680
She's not moving around the world
just cause you're taking a job there!

375
00:21:21.760 --> 00:21:23.720
We could ask for her opinion.

376
00:21:23.800 --> 00:21:24.720
Is it urgent?

377
00:21:25.320 --> 00:21:27.080
Does it have to be right now?

378
00:21:27.160 --> 00:21:29.160
[poignant music continues]

379
00:21:33.200 --> 00:21:34.120
No.

380
00:21:39.880 --> 00:21:41.160
- I'm sorry.
- [David sighs]

381
00:21:41.240 --> 00:21:43.200
No. it's my fault. I'm sorry.

382
00:21:45.280 --> 00:21:47.360
I'm really on edge these days.

383
00:21:48.640 --> 00:21:50.680
It feels so good to be with you.

384
00:21:50.760 --> 00:21:51.960
[sighs]

385
00:21:53.360 --> 00:21:54.920
Are you going in to see him?

386
00:21:57.440 --> 00:21:58.720
I have to.

387
00:21:59.640 --> 00:22:02.080
[monitor beeping]

388
00:22:07.360 --> 00:22:09.040
[Christophe's daughter] Glad you're here.

389
00:22:16.400 --> 00:22:17.240
[kiss]

390
00:22:20.960 --> 00:22:22.240
[exhales emotionally]

391
00:22:25.720 --> 00:22:26.840
[sniffles]

392
00:22:26.920 --> 00:22:27.920
[sighs]

393
00:22:29.160 --> 00:22:30.200
[David] Hey.

394
00:22:31.080 --> 00:22:33.920
That's your old man. Tough as nails. Hm?

395
00:22:34.440 --> 00:22:36.680
You know he never quits.

396
00:22:36.760 --> 00:22:38.600
[Christophe's daughter] I know.

397
00:22:38.680 --> 00:22:40.360
So you know he's going to wake up.

398
00:22:41.520 --> 00:22:42.720
Yeah. Yeah.

399
00:22:48.080 --> 00:22:50.680
- [boyfriend] Do you want to get a coffee?
- Okay. sure.

400
00:22:56.000 --> 00:22:59.440
The man who did this to him.
have you caught him yet?

401
00:23:02.800 --> 00:23:04.480
We're on his trail.

402
00:23:04.560 --> 00:23:06.160
It's just a matter of time.

403
00:23:09.680 --> 00:23:11.040
[suspenseful music playing]

404
00:23:11.120 --> 00:23:12.920
[officer 1 on radio]
<i>Team 3 is being released.</i>

405
00:23:13.840 --> 00:23:16.840
[officer 2 on radio] <i>Hold that position..</i>
<i>Team 5. you're on call at 300.</i>

406
00:23:16.920 --> 00:23:18.480
[man] Okay. guys. it's our shift.

407
00:23:20.000 --> 00:23:21.760
Not much happening. is there?

408
00:23:23.360 --> 00:23:24.720
[ChloÃ©] There's no trace of CL-20

409
00:23:24.800 --> 00:23:27.360
in the apartment
of our ex-soldier boy with the tattoos.

410
00:23:27.440 --> 00:23:31.040
But last night he named the guy
who ordered the operation.

411
00:23:31.120 --> 00:23:32.240
Francis KrÃ¶ller.

412
00:23:32.320 --> 00:23:34.000
A European arms dealer.

413
00:23:34.080 --> 00:23:36.280
For a guy who sells guns.
that's sticking his neck out.

414
00:23:36.360 --> 00:23:39.480
- Attacking a head of the task force?
- Yeah. it seems weird to me too.

415
00:23:39.560 --> 00:23:41.880
We don't have his motive.
It might be personal or who knows.

416
00:23:41.960 --> 00:23:43.840
We are sure that he organized the robbery.

417
00:23:43.920 --> 00:23:45.720
And he's probably got the CL-20.

418
00:23:45.800 --> 00:23:48.400
Section 3. you'll be on standby.
You'll handle the routine stuff.

419
00:23:48.480 --> 00:23:50.960
Section 2. you're supposed to be off
but I want you on KrÃ¶ller.

420
00:23:51.040 --> 00:23:53.200
Intel's pursuing a lead
so let's be ready to move.

421
00:23:53.280 --> 00:23:55.560
Excuse me.
I think Section 1 should be on KrÃ¶ller.

422
00:23:55.640 --> 00:23:58.800
But you've been on standby the whole week.
You just did an operation.

423
00:23:58.880 --> 00:24:01.320
Yeah. that's true. General.
but we have experience with CL-20.

424
00:24:01.400 --> 00:24:03.520
More importantly.
my team usually works with Tanya.

425
00:24:03.600 --> 00:24:05.720
Come on. KrÃ¶ller's a businessman.
not a field operative.

426
00:24:05.800 --> 00:24:08.560
- He won't be wired up to a stack of CL-20.
- Excuse me. ChloÃ©.

427
00:24:08.640 --> 00:24:10.000
Your job is to get intel.

428
00:24:10.080 --> 00:24:11.000
- Am I right?
- Yeah.

429
00:24:11.080 --> 00:24:14.040
Yeah. so it would be a good plan
from now on for you to stay in your lane

430
00:24:14.120 --> 00:24:16.400
and leave tactical decisions
to the tactical guys. okay?

431
00:24:16.480 --> 00:24:18.480
Sure. You just want
to be the one to catch the guy.

432
00:24:18.560 --> 00:24:19.720
I think you missed the point.

433
00:24:19.800 --> 00:24:22.680
Sure. I answer to Ã‰ric and Arnaud.
but everyone here wants to catch him.

434
00:24:22.760 --> 00:24:24.920
- Is that a problem? Should I apologize?
- And your team?

435
00:24:25.000 --> 00:24:26.680
- Those guys need a break!
- Cool it!

436
00:24:26.760 --> 00:24:29.000
- We're all on edge here.
- Sorry for caring about the teams!

437
00:24:29.080 --> 00:24:31.200
Section 1 will be in charge of KrÃ¶ller.

438
00:24:31.280 --> 00:24:33.080
Okay? That's it.

439
00:24:36.600 --> 00:24:37.720
You happy now?

440
00:24:38.640 --> 00:24:39.720
Jerk.

441
00:24:47.680 --> 00:24:49.160
[David] General! General!

442
00:24:52.160 --> 00:24:54.600
I need to talk to you about Max.

443
00:24:54.680 --> 00:24:56.640
Villiers. You know. Laurent's son?

444
00:24:56.720 --> 00:24:58.000
- He just started.
- Yes. Sure.

445
00:24:58.080 --> 00:24:59.920
I'm having a problem with the guy.

446
00:25:00.000 --> 00:25:03.320
In terms of skills. uh. he's fine.
He knows his stuff. he performs.

447
00:25:03.400 --> 00:25:06.080
I'm worried about his personality.
And his behavior.

448
00:25:09.000 --> 00:25:11.120
[sighs] The kid is arrogant.

449
00:25:12.000 --> 00:25:13.000
Full of himself.

450
00:25:13.080 --> 00:25:14.840
He's got a real problem with authority.

451
00:25:14.920 --> 00:25:17.760
- It's always got to be his way.
- Yeah. but you've all got that problem.

452
00:25:19.080 --> 00:25:20.080
General.

453
00:25:20.160 --> 00:25:23.040
He disobeyed a direct order
on his first mission.

454
00:25:23.720 --> 00:25:25.640
So what do you recommend we do? Hm?

455
00:25:26.640 --> 00:25:29.320
We made a mistake
when we admitted him to the unit.

456
00:25:29.400 --> 00:25:31.080
I don't think he belongs in GIGN.

457
00:25:31.160 --> 00:25:34.840
That's going pretty far
for the behavior you're describing.

458
00:25:34.920 --> 00:25:37.080
My view is. don't do it.

459
00:25:37.160 --> 00:25:39.040
But it's your section. Your decision.

460
00:25:39.120 --> 00:25:40.640
Tomorrow we do the trust shooting.

461
00:25:40.720 --> 00:25:43.800
I don't need to remind you.
The point of no return for new recruits.

462
00:25:43.880 --> 00:25:45.360
If you're serious. do it now.

463
00:25:45.440 --> 00:25:48.520
After that. he's one of us
whether you like it or not. okay?

464
00:25:49.000 --> 00:25:50.600
- Fine.
- But. Commander.

465
00:25:51.360 --> 00:25:54.160
Try to leave your emotions out of the job.

466
00:25:54.240 --> 00:25:56.160
No. Wait a minute. General.

467
00:25:56.240 --> 00:25:58.320
He may be Laurent's son and my godson.
but that's got--

468
00:25:58.400 --> 00:26:02.560
No. no. I meanâ€¦ I mean what happened
yesterday after the operation.

469
00:26:06.120 --> 00:26:06.960
Okay.

470
00:26:07.040 --> 00:26:07.920
Good.

471
00:26:10.760 --> 00:26:13.440
[tense music playing]

472
00:26:35.080 --> 00:26:37.080
[music fades]

473
00:26:40.760 --> 00:26:42.920
Excuse me.
I'm looking for. uh. the auditorium.

474
00:26:43.000 --> 00:26:45.800
- Do you know where it is?
- Uh. the big hall? It's down at the end.

475
00:26:45.880 --> 00:26:47.400
- On the left.
- Thanks a lot.

476
00:26:47.480 --> 00:26:50.720
[piano playing
"Impromptu No. 2" by Franz Schubert]

477
00:27:05.200 --> 00:27:06.120
[note sustains]

478
00:27:06.200 --> 00:27:09.680
No. no. no! Don't stop. don't stop.
Play the whole thing! Go on!

479
00:27:09.760 --> 00:27:10.920
No. I can't do it.

480
00:27:11.000 --> 00:27:13.520
[professor] Why can't you?
Ask yourself. why can't you do it?

481
00:27:13.600 --> 00:27:16.400
- Because the piece is too fast for me.
- No. the piece isn't fast!

482
00:27:16.480 --> 00:27:19.560
You can't do it because you haven't
practiced enough. Manon! That's all!

483
00:27:19.640 --> 00:27:21.320
Okay. Let's break for lunch.

484
00:27:23.600 --> 00:27:24.720
[chuckles]

485
00:27:30.800 --> 00:27:31.920
[opens soda can]

486
00:27:32.760 --> 00:27:35.320
So. what was the problem
you were having just now?

487
00:27:35.840 --> 00:27:38.200
Didn't you practice enough.
or is the piece too difficult?

488
00:27:38.280 --> 00:27:42.760
The problem is just that I'm not sure
if I should practice more or not at all.

489
00:27:42.840 --> 00:27:44.240
What do you mean?

490
00:27:46.400 --> 00:27:47.240
Nothing.

491
00:27:47.320 --> 00:27:48.720
Come on. Tell me.

492
00:27:51.280 --> 00:27:53.040
Why'd you come have lunch with me?

493
00:27:53.800 --> 00:27:54.960
You've never done that before.

494
00:27:55.040 --> 00:27:57.520
I came because I felt like seeing you.
That's all.

495
00:27:57.600 --> 00:27:59.400
- That's all?
- Yeah. that's all.

496
00:27:59.480 --> 00:28:01.440
- Okay.
- Okay. what?

497
00:28:01.520 --> 00:28:04.200
- What's that supposed to mean?
- You won't want talk about it.

498
00:28:04.280 --> 00:28:06.440
What? Sure I will.

499
00:28:07.520 --> 00:28:09.320
